# IATA Style FAQ Design Contract\
\
## Visual Atmosphere\
The brand is "Aviation Professional." The layout must be clean, high-contrast, and utilize generous whitespace. Use a two-column layout where appropriate (similar to the checkout reference).\
\
## UI Component Rules\
### 1. Navigation & Headers\
- **Back Link:** Use a simple arrow icon with "Go back to shopping" style text in IATA Blue.\
- **Progress Indicators:** Use the circular "stepper" style found in the reference for multi-part FAQ categories.\
\
### 2. FAQ Accordions (Selection Cards)\
- Items should look like the "Billing Address" card in the reference.\
- **State - Normal:** White background, 1px border (#D1D5DB).\
- **State - Active/Selected:** Light blue tint background, 2px border (#002496), with a blue radio-button style indicator.\
\
### 3. Typography Rules\
- **Main Heading:** "Select billing address" style (Large, Aktiv Grotesk Bold, text-main).\
- **Labels:** Small, bold, all-caps for categories (e.g., "MEMBER DISCOUNT").\
- **Prices/Numbers:** If applicable, use the Green (#34A853) for highlights or "Updated" badges.\
\
### 4. Buttons (Primary Action)\
- **Background:** IATA Blue (#
\f1 \expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
1E32FA
\f0 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 ).\
- **Text:** White, Aktiv Grotesk Bold.\
- **Shape:** Rectangular with very slight 4px rounding.\
\
## Do's and Don'ts\
**Do:**\
- Use the subtle vertical blue line (separator) seen in the footer of the reference.\
- Maintain a clear visual hierarchy between "Question" and "Answer."\
- Include a "Need help? Visit FAQs" style footer.\
\
**Don't:**\
- No drop shadows. Use borders for depth.\
- Use max 4px to round the buttons.\
- Avoid bright colors other than IATA Blue and Success Green.}